05-sam-the-ai-screen: Administration AI AI Which provider this workspace asks, under which models, and whether its content may be sent there at all. Choosing a provider and consenting to use it are two decisions, and both are made here. Provider Choose a provider OpenAI-compatible Ollama None OpenAI-compatible covers OpenAI, Azure, Mistral, vLLM and LiteLLM. Ollama is a model running where you run it. None calls nothing. Address Where the provider is reached. Leave it empty for the provider’s own default. Model for proposals The model that writes titles, notes, breakdowns and summaries, named as the provider names it. Model for meaning The model that turns entries into vectors for search by meaning and for finding look-alikes. Leave it empty to search by words only. API key Sealed as soon as it is saved. Nothing shows it again. Where the provider processes what it is sent Choose where On this installation’s own infrastructure In the European Economic Area In a country with an adequacy decision In a third country Declared by you, recorded with the configuration, and shown to the people whose content goes there. Send this workspace’s content to 127.0.0.1:18199, on this installation’s own infrastructure With this on, an entry’s title and notes, the comments on it, an arrival’s subject and body, and the names of a collection’s labels and columns are sent to the provider named above whenever somebody asks for a proposal, a summary or a search by meaning. Nothing is sent while it is off, and nothing is ever sent without somebody asking. Save Keeping one's own content out Whether each person here may keep what they wrote out of AI. AI stays this workspace's decision; a person can only keep their own content out. In this workspace Each person may keep their own content out of AI AI is part of everybody's work Save Nothing has changed yet. The budget Our own model: today 0 tokens used, with no budget. Counted per day in this workspace's time zone; a budget renews at midnight. Daily budget of our own model In tokens a day. Leave it empty for no budget: the installation's budget never limits our own model. Save the budget Remove the provider The configuration and its sealed key go, and nothing here proposes anything until a provider is configured again. Nothing already accepted is undone. Remove the provider
